What are the most important formulas for parabola in JEE Advanced?

The five most frequently used formulas are: (1) Parametric form: (at², 2at) for y² = 4ax. (2) Equation of tangent at (at², 2at): ty = x + at². (3) Equation of normal: y = mx - 2am - am³. (4) Focal chord condition: t₁t₂ = -1. (5) Length of focal chord: a(t₁ - t₂)².

Is parabola important for JEE Advanced or just JEE Main?

Parabola is important for both, but JEE Advanced tests it at a deeper level. JEE Main focuses on standard formulas like equation of tangent and normal. JEE Advanced combines parabola with circles, loci, and geometric reasoning in multi-step problems requiring 4-6 logical jumps.

How many questions on parabola come in JEE Advanced?

Typically 1-3 questions per year appear on parabola in JEE Advanced, often as part of paragraph-based or multi-correct sets. Between 2009 and 2016, there were 16 questions totalling approximately 52 marks, making it one of the most heavily tested coordinate geometry topics.

Can parabola questions appear in JEE Advanced Paper 2 as well?

Yes. Parabola questions have appeared in both Paper 1 and Paper 2 of JEE Advanced. The 2013 paragraph on focal chords spanned both papers' difficulty profile. Always treat both papers as equally important for coordinate geometry preparation.

How long does it take to prepare parabola for JEE Advanced?

With focused preparation, 10-14 days is sufficient - 3 days on theory and standard results, 4 days on JEE Main-level problems, and 5-7 days on JEE Advanced previous year questions with full solution analysis. Students enrolled in eSaral's Kota-quality online batches typically complete this in structured weekly modules. Leave a comment
